# Unblessed: a Notification Handler writing back to a key it watches (#621); first blessing awaits human review.
# The Handler rounds each score it hears about. Its own write sends it a
# Notification, and the session pumps again at the same Clock reading until a
# Pump leaves no Notification queued: the rounded value changes nothing.
> :grant scores store
> :clock virtual 2026-09-30T10:00:00Z
> on scoresChanged change, queued
|   repeat for each key in the "keys" of change
|     ask scores to get key
|     say key & " = " & it
|     if it is not round(it) then ask scores to set key, round(it)
|   end repeat
| end scoresChanged
> ask scores to watch "rounding", "score/", "scoresChanged"
> ask scores to set "score/alex", 2.6
[session/r3] score/alex = 2.6
[session/r4] score/alex = 3
> ask scores to set "score/alex", 4
[session/r6] score/alex = 4
